; bitwise.xon -- what this project's owl wears.
;
; Bitwise is the ASCII owl in every x source header; x-lang's apps/bitwise
; draws it for a named project, and THIS file is this project's own say in
; how it looks.  The generator reads it during discovery; drop the file and
; the owl goes plain.  Fields, all optional:
;
;   (mascot "LABEL")          shown on the gallery card and in the readout
;   (logo "COLOUR NAME")      printed where the hashed hue would be
;   (accent H S L)            replaces the hashed hue in the field and the eyes
;   (secondary H S L)         the colour for role b
;   (eyes (H S L) (H S L))    two-tone eyes, left then right
;   (rows "ROW" ...)          the owl's glyph rows: printable ASCII, plus lambda and the turtle
;   (roles "ROW" ...)         same shape: i ink, e/f the eyes, a accent, b secondary
;   (reference "LINE")        one line in this project's own language, on the banner

(costume "x-lang"
  (rows "., .," "{OvO}" "(   )" " \" \"")
  (roles "ii ii" "ieifi" "iiiii" " i i ")
  (reference "(def owl '{O,O})"))
